was the moon landing faked the other day  I went with two friends to see first man  the new film about Neil Armstrong and  the moon landing starring Ryan Gosling  and on the way it became pretty clear  that one of these friends of mine wasn't  totally convinced that the moon landings  really happened now I'm sure all of us  know one or more people like this and  people tend to cite all kinds of  different alleged evidence that proves  the landings must have been faked in  this case my friend was caught up on the  idea that the recordings of the  conversations between the astronauts and  Mission Control showed that even though  there should have been a delay of a  certain amount of seconds accounting for  the distance between the Earth and the  moon one of the astronauts responses was  too quick proving that they were in  reality back on earth where there is no  delay  I'm not going to debunk every single  conspiracy theory related to this  including supposed unexplainable shadows  the apparent movement of the American  flag and others and the reason why is  that those debunking zhh are readily  available online NASA itself has issued  rebuttals Mythbusters did a whole  episode on the subject and there are  substantial third party evidence for the  landings you can even just read the  Wikipedia article on it and check the  sources in the links I just want to shed  light on one specific point in order for  there to have been a conspiracy in the  moon landings literally about four  hundred and eleven thousand people would  have had to have been in on it this was  the number of people working on the  program mostly engineers scientists and  technicians and that is the number of  people that would have had to remain  silent since July 1969 in order to keep  the truth a secret and so I would say  that the idea that the moon landings  were faked is so unlikely as to be  considered completely implausible in the  end it was infinitely easier to actually  land on the moon than to try to fake it  and cover it up
 

